WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:04.710
"The Walking Dead — Daryl Dixon" throws
a fan-favorite character across an ocean,

00:00:04.710 --> 00:00:09.890
introduces a new dynamic, and leaves our hero
between a metaphorical rock and a hard place.

00:00:09.890 --> 00:00:12.520
Here's what the ending of season one means.

00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:17.140
Early on in "The Walking Dead: Daryl Dixon,"
Daryl manages to break free from his captors

00:00:17.140 --> 00:00:21.550
and starts wandering France — searching
for a way home, running into some new walker

00:00:21.550 --> 00:00:25.120
variants, and meeting plenty of new characters
along the way.

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:29.699
Where the original series focused on Daryl's
transformation from a "lone wolf" survivalist

00:00:29.699 --> 00:00:34.570
to a beloved leader and a surrogate father
figure to R.J. and Judith Grimes, "Daryl Dixon"

00:00:34.570 --> 00:00:39.050
explores this newfound empathy as Daryl becomes
the protector of a young boy named Laurent.

00:00:39.050 --> 00:00:43.710
Laurent is a young boy who was born via C-section
after his mother had already turned into a

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:48.419
zombie, and who is now revered as the Messiah
by a religious network called the "Union of Hope."

00:00:48.419 --> 00:00:53.050
Members of the Union believe Laurent is destined
to end the apocalypse and restore humanity

00:00:53.050 --> 00:00:54.621
to its former glory.

00:00:54.621 --> 00:00:57.729
"If we're wrong at least you will have helped
a boy get to a better place.

00:00:57.729 --> 00:00:59.080
But if we're right…

00:00:59.801 --> 00:01:00.989
Why not bet on hope?"

00:01:00.989 --> 00:01:04.830
In a storyline that draws some parallels to
that of "The Last of Us," Daryl agrees to

00:01:04.830 --> 00:01:09.850
transport this young savior across France
to the Union's base, though in Episode 5,

00:01:09.850 --> 00:01:14.350
Daryl, Laurent, Laurent's father Quinn, and
the nun Isabelle are captured by agents of

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:15.170
the Pouvoir.

00:01:15.170 --> 00:01:19.710
The episode ends on a cliffhanger, in which
Daryl is forced into a gladiator fight against

00:01:19.710 --> 00:01:24.220
the enhanced walkers created by the Pouvoir,
while some members of the Union sneak into

00:01:24.220 --> 00:01:28.329
the Pouvoir's arena to stage a desperate rescue
attempt.

00:01:28.329 --> 00:01:32.461
The finale of "The Walking Dead: Daryl Dixon
” begins inside the gladiator pit, where

00:01:32.461 --> 00:01:36.270
Daryl quickly defeats a few of the Pouvoir's
genetically enhanced walkers.

00:01:36.270 --> 00:01:40.259
Quinn is sent in and chained to Daryl to provide
more of a challenge, though the pair still

00:01:40.259 --> 00:01:44.020
manage to defeat wave after wave of these
new and improved zombies.

00:01:44.020 --> 00:01:48.579
Their success draws a surprising amount of
support from the crowd, who start cheering

00:01:48.579 --> 00:01:50.219
"Dixon" as Daryl and Quinn fight.

00:01:50.219 --> 00:01:54.420
The enraged Pouvoir leader Genet decides to
execute Daryl and Quinn before things get

00:01:54.420 --> 00:01:58.770
out of hand, but they're saved by a well-timed
bullet which kicks off a full-blown uproar

00:01:58.770 --> 00:02:00.219
inside the arena.

00:02:00.219 --> 00:02:04.500
In the ensuing chaos, Daryl and Quinn escape
their chains and Quinn reveals that he was

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:06.390
infected during their battle.

00:02:06.390 --> 00:02:10.539
Quinn sacrifices himself to make way for Daryl
and Laurent's escape, declaring his love for

00:02:10.539 --> 00:02:15.840
Isabelle — his former lover and Laurent's
biological aunt, who raised Laurent in Quinn's absence.

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:20.960
Daryl and his Union allies rush to free Isabelle
and Laurent from Pouvoir custody, though during

00:02:20.960 --> 00:02:25.548
the final stage of their escape, they come
face-to-face with the reanimated corpse of Quinn.

00:02:25.548 --> 00:02:29.410
In a heartbreaking turn of events, Laurent
is forced to kill the walker who was once

00:02:29.410 --> 00:02:32.510
his father, saving Isabelle and later declaring:

00:02:32.510 --> 00:02:34.530
"It wasn't him anymore.

00:02:34.530 --> 00:02:38.040
That man was never my father."

00:02:38.040 --> 00:02:41.750
With Quinn put down for good, the group completes
their escape from the arena and splits up

00:02:41.750 --> 00:02:42.490
on the road.

00:02:42.490 --> 00:02:46.809
Fallou and Emile depart into the woods while
the rest flee towards Mont Saint-Michel.

00:02:46.809 --> 00:02:51.320
Along the way, Isabelle confesses to Daryl
that she invented a good deal of Laurent's

00:02:51.320 --> 00:02:55.310
"Messianic" powers, hoping to impress Daryl
and draw support for the Union.

00:02:55.310 --> 00:02:59.629
Oddly, this brief confession is juxtaposed
with a roadside ambush from Pouvoir agents

00:02:59.629 --> 00:03:04.510
led by Stéphane Codron, where Laurent displays
an eerie level of persuasion that borders

00:03:04.510 --> 00:03:05.971
on the supernatural.

00:03:05.971 --> 00:03:11.360
Laurent imparts a "message from God" and somehow
convinces Codron to gun down his fellow agent,

00:03:11.360 --> 00:03:15.250
allowing Isabelle, Daryl, and Laurent to continue
on their way.

00:03:15.250 --> 00:03:19.650
Finally, the trio arrives in the fortified
city of Mont Saint-Michel, where the religious

00:03:19.650 --> 00:03:21.680
haven known as "The Nest" resides.

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:25.170
Despite all that he went through to protect
Laurent and deliver the boy safely to The

00:03:25.170 --> 00:03:30.069
Nest, Daryl still has his heart set on a return
to America, and he departs in the night against

00:03:30.069 --> 00:03:31.449
Isabelle's protests.

00:03:31.449 --> 00:03:35.360
After a brief stop in Normandy, Daryl boards
a boat on Omaha Beach.

00:03:35.360 --> 00:03:39.519
He is about to set sail when he hears someone
calling his name, and discovers that Laurent

00:03:39.519 --> 00:03:42.100
had followed him in order to say a proper
goodbye.

00:03:42.100 --> 00:03:46.870
Unfortunately, his calls also have attracted
a fresh horde of walkers, and thus the first

00:03:46.870 --> 00:03:51.379
season of "Daryl Dixon" ends with a cliffhanger
as Daryl has to choose whether to set sail

00:03:51.379 --> 00:03:53.559
or turn back to save Laurent.

00:03:53.559 --> 00:03:58.189
Despite being a brutal murderer and a sworn
enemy to Daryl Dixon, Stéphane is visibly

00:03:58.189 --> 00:04:02.430
conflicted when Genet gives him the orders
to kill Laurent, and his resolve crumbles

00:04:02.430 --> 00:04:04.869
when faced with actually murdering the child.

00:04:04.869 --> 00:04:09.040
After returning to the Pouvoir hideout of
Maison Mère, Stephan attempts to lie his

00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:12.989
way out of Genet's interrogation when he returns
without Daryl or Laurent.

00:04:12.989 --> 00:04:16.940
Unfortunately for him, she doesn't believe
any of it, and orders her agents to torture

00:04:16.940 --> 00:04:18.430
him for more information.

00:04:18.430 --> 00:04:22.270
While Daryl Dixon and his comrades may have
escaped the wrath of Genet for now, their

00:04:22.270 --> 00:04:26.290
fate now hinges on Stéphane's ability to
withstand torture — since he is one of the

00:04:26.290 --> 00:04:29.520
few people who knows the secret location of
"The Nest."

00:04:29.520 --> 00:04:34.360
Considering the gross levels of human experimentation
that Genet and the rest of the Pouvoir have

00:04:34.360 --> 00:04:38.229
demonstrated, it's unlikely that Stéphane
will be able to hold out forever.

00:04:38.229 --> 00:04:42.020
This perfectly sets up the impending conflict
between The Nest and the surviving members

00:04:42.020 --> 00:04:48.190
of the Pouvoir, something that will likely
be a major focus in "Daryl Dixon" Season 2.

00:04:48.190 --> 00:04:53.130
Most exciting to some longtime fans, the episode's
final moments reunite fans with "The Walking

00:04:53.130 --> 00:04:54.590
Dead" staple Carol.

00:04:54.590 --> 00:04:58.520
Just before the credits roll, the episode
cuts away to Freeport, Maine, where an unnamed

00:04:58.520 --> 00:05:01.270
drifter is seen riding Daryl's iconic motorcycle.

00:05:01.270 --> 00:05:05.979
The cyclist is pursued by Carol, and after
a brief scuffle, she knocks him unconscious

00:05:05.979 --> 00:05:06.979
with a wrench.

00:05:06.979 --> 00:05:10.480
She interrogates him and discovers that he
bought the motorcycle from survivors living

00:05:10.480 --> 00:05:15.440
further up the road, and she locks him in
the trunk before riding off on Daryl's motorcycle.

00:05:15.440 --> 00:05:18.930
Any "Walking Dead" fan will know that Carol
and Daryl are closer than perhaps any other

00:05:18.930 --> 00:05:22.600
characters in the entire series, and have
been there for each other through more than

00:05:22.600 --> 00:05:24.460
a decade of strife and heartbreak.

00:05:24.460 --> 00:05:29.020
Despite never pursuing a romantic relationship,
they professed their love for each other before

00:05:29.020 --> 00:05:31.380
Daryl left in the original series' finale.

00:05:31.380 --> 00:05:35.370
Now, love has driven Carol to seek out her
friend after his disappearance — picking

00:05:35.370 --> 00:05:38.940
up the trail in Maine, and setting up her
return for the next season of "The Walking

00:05:38.940 --> 00:05:40.410
Dead: Daryl Dixon."

00:05:40.410 --> 00:05:44.530
After leaving their relationship up in the
air in the original series finale, this reunion

00:05:44.530 --> 00:05:47.639
could herald a true happy ending for both
Daryl and Carol.

00:05:47.639 --> 00:05:51.440
Either way, we'll definitely be seeing more
of her—the second season has been announced

00:05:51.440 --> 00:05:54.970
as "The Walking Dead: Daryl Dixon — The
Book of Carol."

00:05:54.970 --> 00:05:59.130
While much of "Daryl Dixon" Season 1 centers
around Daryl's survival and desire to fight

00:05:59.130 --> 00:06:03.280
his way home to his family, the finale helps
to clarify that the series is also a very

00:06:03.280 --> 00:06:08.770
dysfunctional father-son story — one that
is bogged down by a long history of family trauma.

00:06:08.770 --> 00:06:09.770
"Sounds hard."

00:06:09.910 --> 00:06:10.910
"It was.

00:06:11.070 --> 00:06:12.070
When he was around.

00:06:13.031 --> 00:06:14.299
Which was hardly ever."

00:06:14.600 --> 00:06:18.470
Throughout both the original "The Walking
Dead" series and "Daryl Dixon" we learn that

00:06:18.470 --> 00:06:23.669
Daryl's father was extremely abusive and neglectful,
and that he was hardly ever there for him

00:06:23.669 --> 00:06:25.000
or his brother Merle.

00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:29.310
In a rare moment of vulnerability, Daryl tells
Isabelle that his grandfather had neglected

00:06:29.310 --> 00:06:33.740
Daryl's father as well, and hints at the generational
trauma that has been passed down through the

00:06:33.740 --> 00:06:34.870
Dixon family.

00:06:34.870 --> 00:06:38.849
Now, this trauma threatens the development
of another young boy — Laurent, to whom

00:06:38.849 --> 00:06:41.169
Daryl has become a pseudo-father figure.

00:06:41.169 --> 00:06:45.631
The series tells us as much during the final
confrontation between Quinn and Laurent, where

00:06:45.631 --> 00:06:50.150
Daryl encourages Laurent to kill his father's
reanimated body, and Laurent disowns his true

00:06:50.150 --> 00:06:51.849
father once and for all.

00:06:51.849 --> 00:06:55.580
When Daryl leaves in the middle of the night,
Isabelle boldly calls him out for repeating

00:06:55.580 --> 00:06:59.830
the cycle of father-son abandonment that left
him so dysfunctional in the first place.

00:06:59.830 --> 00:07:03.729
Thus, when Laurent arrives on the beach he
forces Daryl to finally confront the trauma

00:07:03.729 --> 00:07:05.260
left behind by his father.

00:07:05.260 --> 00:07:09.691
Will Daryl end up breaking the cycle and remaining
by Laurent's side as a real father figure?

00:07:09.691 --> 00:07:14.610
Or will he succumb to the same weakness that
caused his own substantial abandonment issues?

00:07:14.610 --> 00:07:18.759
Although this season finale places a heavy
emphasis on Daryl Dixon's attachment issues

00:07:18.759 --> 00:07:22.919
and his newfound connection to Laurent, some
fans online aren't too thrilled about this

00:07:22.919 --> 00:07:26.650
"family trauma" storyline that the show has
thrust into Daryl's lap.

00:07:26.650 --> 00:07:31.069
As pointed out by many fans on Reddit, Daryl
has already served as a surrogate father figure

00:07:31.069 --> 00:07:36.380
for R.J. and Judith Grimes, essentially raising
both of them after Rick Grimes' disappearance

00:07:36.380 --> 00:07:37.439
in Season 9.

00:07:37.439 --> 00:07:42.199
This somewhat invalidates Isabelle's argument
about "repeating the cycle," since staying

00:07:42.199 --> 00:07:44.690
in France would be an act of abandonment in
itself.

00:07:44.690 --> 00:07:49.050
"You think you are escaping history by doing
this but you are not.

00:07:49.050 --> 00:07:50.390
You're repeating it."

00:07:50.390 --> 00:07:54.710
As such, one could argue that Daryl's "abandonment
issues" concern his true family rather than

00:07:54.710 --> 00:07:56.169
his newfound French allies.

00:07:56.169 --> 00:08:01.400
To truly conquer his history of family dysfunction,
Daryl will need to return to America and resume

00:08:01.400 --> 00:08:04.120
his role as the father figure to the Grimes
children.

00:08:04.120 --> 00:08:08.690
If this explanation holds any weight, it could
set up a very interesting conflict for Season

00:08:08.690 --> 00:08:12.659
2 of "Daryl Dixon" — wherein Laurent and
his religious allies attempt to stop Daryl

00:08:12.659 --> 00:08:15.719
from returning to where he arguably truly
belongs.

00:08:15.719 --> 00:08:20.030
While the ending of "Daryl Dixon" primarily
serves as a setup for the series' forthcoming

00:08:20.030 --> 00:08:24.280
second season, it's important to clarify how
this season finale could tie into the rest

00:08:24.280 --> 00:08:25.710
of the franchise as a whole.

00:08:25.710 --> 00:08:30.159
Because Daryl is still in France at the end
of the series, this finale also makes it extremely

00:08:30.159 --> 00:08:34.039
unlikely that we'll see Daryl in the upcoming
"Rick and Michonne" spinoff – something

00:08:34.039 --> 00:08:39.080
which will no doubt disappoint plenty of fans,
since his original goal was to track down Rick Grimes.

00:08:39.080 --> 00:08:42.959
On top of that, it's important to note that
both Negan and Maggie Rhee find themselves

00:08:42.959 --> 00:08:45.540
in Manhattan in"The Walking Dead: Dead City."

00:08:45.540 --> 00:08:49.430
If Daryl does return to America, it's not
out of the question that we'll see him and

00:08:49.430 --> 00:08:54.019
Carol overshoot their destination and wind
up further down the East Coast — potentially

00:08:54.019 --> 00:08:56.909
making a cameo in "Dead City" Season 2.

00:08:56.909 --> 00:09:01.720
While some fans online were entirely unenthusiastic
about the way this finale put pressure on

00:09:01.720 --> 00:09:05.790
Daryl Dixon to stay with Laurent, showrunner
David Zabel says that he had planned this

00:09:05.790 --> 00:09:07.029
ending from the start.

00:09:07.029 --> 00:09:09.240
Zabel explained during an interview with TheWrap,

00:09:09.240 --> 00:09:11.430
"That was really my first pitch on the story.

00:09:11.430 --> 00:09:15.030
At that point — he's not going to say it
because he's not that kind of guy — he is

00:09:15.030 --> 00:09:16.950
like, 'I know I've got to do this.

00:09:16.950 --> 00:09:18.410
This is an obligation.

00:09:18.410 --> 00:09:21.699
Regardless of what I want for myself, I've
got to do this thing.'"

00:09:21.839 --> 00:09:26.180
Zabel went on to say that this inner conflict
is hinted at earlier in the episode when Daryl

00:09:26.180 --> 00:09:28.040
is trying to leave in the middle of the night.

00:09:28.040 --> 00:09:32.320
Zabel explained that Norman Reedus chose to
play that scene with demonstrative frustration,

00:09:32.320 --> 00:09:37.179
angrily throwing supplies into his bag because
he is torn on whether or not he should really leave.

00:09:37.179 --> 00:09:40.940
Though this cliffhanger ending might not sit
well with some fans, it's clear that both

00:09:40.940 --> 00:09:45.690
Zabel and Reedus wanted to emphasize Daryl
Dixon's inner turmoil when he finally arrives

00:09:45.690 --> 00:09:49.440
on that beach — having discovered a new
kind of family, and nearly abandoning them

00:09:49.440 --> 00:09:51.290
when they need him most.

00:09:51.290 --> 00:09:54.990
It's safe to say that many fans were probably
disappointed when it was announced that the

00:09:54.990 --> 00:10:00.480
rumored "Daryl and Carol" spinoff series would
be moving forward with only one of those characters.

00:10:00.480 --> 00:10:04.200
On top of the fact that they are both fan-favorite
characters who have been around since Season

00:10:04.200 --> 00:10:08.850
1, their chemistry together is one of the
undisputed highlights of the entire series.

00:10:08.850 --> 00:10:12.660
Daryl's solemn journey overseas through France
feels a little bit lonely when you remember

00:10:12.660 --> 00:10:16.370
he was supposed to be accompanied by his best
friend, though "The Walking Dead" primary

00:10:16.370 --> 00:10:21.440
director Greg Nicotero says there was an unseen
benefit in removing her from Season 1.

00:10:21.440 --> 00:10:24.030
He explained during an interview with TV Insider,

00:10:24.030 --> 00:10:28.050
"I think having the show concentrate on Daryl
specifically and his experiences, to lay the

00:10:28.050 --> 00:10:32.800
groundwork for that and then to bring Carol
in later, it allows for richer storytelling.

00:10:32.800 --> 00:10:36.310
It just doesn't rely on two characters that
you already know because then there are less

00:10:36.310 --> 00:10:37.570
places to go.

00:10:37.570 --> 00:10:39.450
I think it allowed Daryl to grow."

00:10:39.450 --> 00:10:43.579
Nicotero went on to clarify that the return
of actress Melissa McBride in the finale is

00:10:43.579 --> 00:10:48.139
also a boon for the series, since both McBride
and Norman Reedus will have a good deal of

00:10:48.139 --> 00:10:50.800
involvement with the development of Carol
and Daryl's next chapter.

00:10:50.800 --> 00:10:55.389
As for what that next chapter will hold, fans
will just have to wait until "The Book of

00:10:55.389 --> 00:10:57.701
Carol" drops in 2024.

